      "title": "Position Overview",
      "description": "Job Opportunities |             RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Enterprise Reporting Analyst |             RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES page has loaded. Enterprise Reporting Analyst |             RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Enterprise Reporting Analyst Print Apply ﻿ Enterprise Reporting Analyst Salary $55,000.00 - $60,000.00 Annually Location Lawrenceville Job Type Full-Time Job Number Rider00376 Division Enrollment Management Department Enrollment Management Administration Opening Date 07/08/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University invites applications for an Enterprise Reporting Analyst.    Reporting to the Assistant Vice President of Enrollment Operations, the Enterprise Reporting Analyst designs, develops, and delivers reports, dashboards, and data visualizations that support functional users and institutional leadership across Enrollment Management and other administrative areas. This position transforms complex institutional data into clear, actionable reporting products that support operational decision-making, planning, and performance monitoring. The role serves as a reporting partner to campus stakeholders by gathering requirements, translating business needs into technical reporting solutions, and delivering accurate and timely dashboards and reports across multiple enterprise systems. The Enterprise Reporting Analyst ensures reporting consistency, usability, and reliability through validation, collaboration, and ongoing refinement of reporting tools. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience Bachelor’s degree in a related field. 3–5 years of experience in reporting, data analysis, or business intelligence in a higher education or ERP environment. Strong SQL skills for querying and reporting from an enterprise data warehouse or Operational Data Store (ODS). Experience with Ellucian Banner (Student, Financial Aid, Finance, or related modules) or comparable ERP systems. Experience developing reports and dashboards using IBM Cognos Analytics or similar enterprise reporting tools. Ability to gather, document, and translate business requirements into reporting solutions and deliverables. Experience validating and reconciling data. Strong analytical skills with attention to detail, data integrity, and reporting logic. Ability to manage multiple reporting requests and deadlines. Experience collaborating with functional offices. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Experience with Cognos Framework Manager, report authoring, or query development in an enterprise environment Experience working in a higher education Institutional Research, Enrollment Management Analytics, or central reporting environment. Familiarity with FERPA and higher education data security and reporting standards. Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit https://www.rider.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/benefits/overview-employee-benefits/full-time-administrative-employees Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES Job Opportunities Menu Close Menu RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES Job Opportunities Email Job Alerts Rider University Website Help & Support Translate SOCIAL Twitter LinkedIn Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our 