ss with the support of the University community. Position Overview The Department of Teacher Education at Rider University seeks an adjunct instructor of literacy for multilingual learners for the Fall 2026 semester beginning September 9, 2026. This position is to teach EDU 358: Literacy and the Bilingual/Bicultural Child. Salary is $4,215.98 for a 3-credit course.  Please note that a full course is considered to have 9 students enrolled in the course.   If a section is not full, 8 or fewer enrollees, the salary is prorated based on the number of students enrolled in the course. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience Master's degree in Education Education & expertise in bilingual/multilingual education and literacy instruction Demonstrated knowledge of strategies to support literacy development in elementary education settings Demonstrated teaching experience of elementary or middle school grades, including the teaching of literacy and multilingual students Demonstrated ability to support pre-service teachers in creating and implementing lessons. Availability to teach on campus on Tuesdays from 4:30-7:10 pm Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Graduate degree in literacy education Experience as an instructor in higher education Experience teaching at the college level with teacher candidates Expertise in teaching multilingual students in elementary schools Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statem