nizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University seeks a temporary Plumber who will maintain and repair plumbing systems and fixtures on campus, which includes toilets, sinks, showers and occasionally underground systems, including but not limited to irrigationlines.    The Plumber will maintain boilers and other mechanical systems and order supplies as needed. The work schedule for this temporary position is Monday - Friday, 7:30 a.m. – 4:00 p.m. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience General knowledge of plumbing systems, fixtures, and installation of these fixtures. Valid driver’s license and satisfactory driving record. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Licensed plumber 5 years of plumbing experience Attendance in VoTech School with a major in Plumbing Knowledge of swimming pool operation or CPO Certification a plus Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish