ncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview The Department of Performing Arts at Rider University seeks an adjunct instructor of Theatre and Musical Theatre for the fall semester beginning September 9, 2026 and the spring semester beginning January 25, 2027. This position is to teach a variety of courses in the BFA Acting curriculum. Salary is $4,215.98 for a 3-credit course.  Please note that a full course is considered to have 9 students enrolled in the course.   If a section is not full, 8 or fewer enrollees, the salary is prorated based on the number of students enrolled in the course. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience BA or BFA in theatre, a related degree field, or equivalent professional experience. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience MFA in Acting Experience working with early-career professionals in theatre and/or musical theatre Experience teaching in a university. Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Acc