      "description": "Job Opportunities |             RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Adjunct Faculty - Musical Theatre |             RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES page has loaded. Adjunct Faculty - Musical Theatre |             RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Adjunct Faculty - Musical Theatre Print Apply ﻿ Adjunct Faculty - Musical Theatre Location Lawrenceville Job Type Part-Time Job Number Rider00369 Division Academic Affairs Department Performing Arts Opening Date 06/22/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit AAUP Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview The Department of Performing Arts at Rider University seeks adjunct instructors of Musical Theatre for the fall semester beginning September 9, 2026. Applicants will be considered for various classes related to Dance, Voice, and Musical Theatre Directing. Salary is $4,215.98 for a 3-credit course.  Please note that a full course is considered to have 9 students enrolled in the course.   If a section is not full, 8 or fewer enrollees, the salary is prorated based on the number of students enrolled in the course. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience BA or BFA in musical theatre, theatre, voice, a related degree field, or equivalent professional experience. Experience directing, teaching, and/or performing in musicals, plays, or other performance genres. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Advanced or Terminal degree in musical theatre, theatre, voice, a related field, or equivalent professional experience. Extensive experience at the national and international level. Experience working with early-career professionals in musical theatre. Experience teaching in a university. Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act,