      "description": "Job Opportunities |             RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Associate Director of Undergraduate Admission |             RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES page has loaded. Associate Director of Undergraduate Admission |             RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Associate Director of Undergraduate Admission Print Apply ﻿ Associate Director of Undergraduate Admission Salary $50,000.00 - $54,000.00 Annually Location Lawrenceville Job Type Full-Time Job Number Rider00371 Division Enrollment Management Department Admissions Opening Date 06/25/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University invites applications for an Associate Director of Undergraduate Admission.  The Associate Director of Undergraduate Admission plays a key leadership role in advancing enrollment goals through strategic recruitment, territory management, and staff development. Reporting to the Director of Undergraduate Admission, this position is responsible for managing a recruitment territory, overseeing Division I athletic recruitment operations, and supervising a team of admission counselors and coordinators. The Associate Director collaborates closely with coaches, academic departments, student affairs, and enrollment leadership to attract, enroll, and retain a diverse and talented student body aligned with the institution's mission and values. Key Responsibilities: Develop and execute strategic recruitment plans to meet undergraduate enrollment objectives. Manage assigned recruitment territories, including travel, relationship building with high schools and community organizations, application review, and yield initiatives. Represent the college at recruitment events, college fairs, open houses, and admitted student programs. Analyze enrollment trends and market data to inform recruitment strategies and territory planning. Participate in holistic application review and admission decision-making processes. Coordinate admission review and communication processes for prospective student-athletes. Advise coaches on admission requirements, timelines, and institutional policies. Perform pre-reads for coaches during their recruitment process. Monitor athletic recruitment pipelines and maintain accurate records to support enrollment forecasting. Collaborate with athletics leadership to support recruitment strategies that align with institutional enrollment goals and NCAA regulations. Facilitate efficient communication among coaches, admission staff, and prospective student-athletes and their families. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience Bachelor's degree Minimum of 5 years of experience in college admission, enrollment management, higher education, athletics recruitment, or a related field. Experience working with NCAA Division I athletics recruitment and enrollment processes. Experience managing large-scale recruitment or campus events. Demonstrated experience supervising professional and/or student staff. Strong organizational, communication, and relationship-building skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to analyze enrollment data and make data-informed decisions. Commitment to inclusive excellence and exceptional customer service. Willingness to travel extensively and work evenings and weekends as needed. Valid driver's license in good standing and vehicle required or have reliable transportation to carry out travel requirements of the position. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Master's degree in higher education, student affairs, business administration, communications, or a related field. Familiarity with CRM systems such as Slate Bilingual Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit https://www.rider.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/benefits/overview-employee-benefits/full-time-administrative-employees Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do 