      "description": "Job Opportunities |             RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Senior Associate Director of Admission Campus Visit Experiences |             RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES page has loaded. Senior Associate Director of Admission Campus Visit Experiences |             RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Senior Associate Director of Admission Campus Visit Experiences Print Apply ﻿ Senior Associate Director of Admission Campus Visit Experiences Salary $60,000.00 - $63,000.00 Annually Location Lawrenceville Job Type Full-Time Job Number Rider00374 Division Enrollment Management Department Admissions Opening Date 07/01/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits We take pride in the ever-evolving nature of our work, which transforms the lives of our students, preparing them for personal and professional success. Rider University is consistently recognized by The Prin ceton Review and U.S. News & World Report as a best college, and as a best-value institution. With more than 100 majors, minors and programs, 19 Division I athletic teams and 150-plus clubs and organizations, Rider Broncs create their own pathways to success with the support of the University community. Position Overview Rider University invites applications for a Senior Associate Director of Admission Campus Visit Experiences.  The Senior Associate Director provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for all prospective student and family visit experiences within the Office of Undergraduate Admissions. This position is responsible for the design, execution, and continuous improvement of campus visit programs that serve as critical recruitment and enrollment tools.  The Senior Associate Director oversees daily visit operations, manages student and professional staff, develops signature on-campus events, and ensures that every visitor interaction reflects the university's mission, values, and commitment to exceptional hospitality. This role collaborates closely with academic departments, student affairs, enrollment management, and campus partners to create engaging and impactful experiences for prospective students and their families. Key Responsibilities: Develop and implement a comprehensive strategy for all undergraduate admission visit programs, including daily information sessions, campus tours, classroom visit opportunities, group visits, and specialty visit programs. Evaluate and enhance visitor experiences using data, surveys, and enrollment outcomes. Ensure all visit experiences align with institutional enrollment goals and brand standards. Monitor industry trends and best practices in campus visit programming and student recruitment. Direct all aspects of the tour guide program, lead tour guide program, front desk ambassadors, and coordinators for the Bronc for a Day program. Recruit, hire, train, supervise, evaluate, and develop a diverse team of student workers for the various roles in the office. Design and facilitate ongoing training focused on customer service, storytelling, university knowledge, and public speaking. Oversee the university's classroom visit program, coordinating with faculty, academic departments, and campus partners. Supervise front desk ambassadors for welcoming guests and supporting admissions operations. Establish service standards and protocols that promote a professional, welcoming, and inclusive environment. Lead the planning and execution of major on-campus recruitment events, including open houses, admitted student programs, counselor events, and specialty visit experiences. Utilize CRM and visit management systems to monitor participation, visitor engagement, and program effectiveness. Analyze visit-related metrics, survey results, and enrollment outcomes to inform decision-making and resource allocation. Required Knowledge, Skills and Experience Bachelor's degree Five or more years of experience in admissions, enrollment management, student affairs, event management, hospitality, or a related field. Experience managing large-scale recruitment or campus events. Demonstrated experience supervising professional and/or student staff. Strong organizational, project management, and event planning skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Commitment to inclusive excellence and exceptional customer service. Willingness to travel extensively and work evenings and weekends as needed. Valid driver's license in good standing and vehicle required or have reliable transportation to carry out travel requirements of the position. Satisfactory background and/or DMV checks required. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Experience Master's degree in higher education, student affairs, business administration, communications, or a related field. Familiarity with CRM systems such as Slate and campus visit management platforms. Bilingual Rider University is committed to fostering an inclusive, vibrant living and learning community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Rider University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. For additional information regarding our Benefits visit https://www.rider.edu/about/offices-services/human-resources/benefits/overview-employee-benefits/full-time-administrative-employees Employer Rider University Address 2083 Lawrenceville Road Lawrenceville, New Jersey, 08648-3099 Phone 609-896-5000 Website https://www.rider.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES Job Opportunities Menu Close Menu RIDER UNIVERSITY CAREER OPPORTUNITIES Job Opportunities Email Job Alerts Rider University Website Help & Support Translate SOCIAL Twitter LinkedIn Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Re